=== Prompt for HW-004 (attempt 1) ===
Implement user story HW-004: Implement formatDate() utility with vitest tests

## Story Description
Create formatDate.ts in the project root. Export a single function `export function formatDate(date: Date, format: 'short' | 'long'): string` that returns: 'short' → 'YYYY-MM-DD' (e.g. '2026-06-04'); 'long' → 'Month DD, YYYY' (e.g. 'June 4, 2026'). Use UTC date components so results are deterministic regardless of host timezone (new Date('2026-06-04') is UTC midnight). For an invalid Date (e.g. new Date('not-a-date')), throw a descriptive Error rather than returning 'NaN'-laden output. Create formatDate.test.ts in the project root with at least 6 vitest tests covering both formats, edge cases (month boundaries, single-digit days), and invalid-Date input. Do not modify any existing files.

## Acceptance Criteria
- formatDate.ts exists in the project root and exports `function formatDate(date: Date, format: 'short' | 'long'): string` (named export, exact signature)
- formatDate(new Date('2026-06-04'), 'short') returns '2026-06-04'
- formatDate(new Date('2026-06-04'), 'long') returns 'June 4, 2026'
- Short format zero-pads month and day: formatDate(new Date('2026-01-05'), 'short') returns '2026-01-05'
- Long format does not pad the day: formatDate(new Date('2026-01-05'), 'long') returns 'January 5, 2026'
- Date components are derived via UTC accessors (getUTCFullYear/getUTCMonth/getUTCDate or equivalent) so tests pass in any host timezone
- Passing an invalid Date throws an Error whose message identifies the problem, and a test asserts the message content with expect(...).toThrow(/invalid date/i) (or an equivalent matcher on the message), not just a bare expect(...).toThrow()
- formatDate.test.ts exists in the project root with at least 6 vitest tests, including at least one month-boundary case (e.g. Dec 31 / Jan 1) and one single-digit-day case in each format
- npx tsc --noEmit exits 0
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing (the new tests pass and no pre-existing tests break)
- git status shows no modifications to existing files — only formatDate.ts and formatDate.test.ts are added
- Long-format month names come from a fixed English month-name array (or a formatter explicitly pinned to locale 'en-US' and timeZone 'UTC'), so output does not vary with the host's ICU/locale build; at least one test covers a month other than January or June (e.g. December)
- Invalid-Date detection works for any Invalid Date regardless of construction: both new Date('not-a-date') and new Date(NaN) throw (i.e. detection is based on Number.isNaN(date.getTime()) or equivalent, not on parsing the input string)
- A leap-day case is covered: formatDate(new Date('2024-02-29'), 'short') returns '2024-02-29' and formatDate(new Date('2024-02-29'), 'long') returns 'February 29, 2024'
- vitest run reports at least 6 more passing tests than the pre-change baseline (i.e. formatDate.test.ts is actually discovered by the existing vitest include patterns, not silently skipped — a green run with an unchanged test count does NOT satisfy this criterion)

